Ze-Reviewed-Against: github.com/gokrazy/tools v0.0.0-20261026191944-942a8faaca93

Upstream pull request: none opened yet.

Ze embeds gok through gok.Context.Execute. Host-side os.Exit and log.Fatal
skip the caller's deferred working-directory restoration and removal of the
prepared instance, leaving the update token and private TLS material behind.
The requirement is stated by writeGokUpdate in internal/appliance/build_update.go:
"The caller MUST remove that instance after gok returns, including on build failure."

Return packing, ELF validation and privileged-helper errors through every Main
caller. Preserve successful helper completion as a distinct typed result through
the public embedded API and all image/VM postwork; only the enclosing command
may map it to success after deferred cleanup. Join the sudo child in the
ordinary return path. Buffer the single DNS result so a packing error cannot
strand its sender. Runtime log.Fatal calls inside the generated appliance init
template are unchanged.

The interaction hint redacts URL passwords rather than printing the updater
credential to the build log, including after successful image preparation.

Terminate both packed kernel command-line formats with a newline after their
reserved space, so runtime boot-file edits have a complete final line. The
regression reads both actual FAT files and preserves their reserved padding.

Design: docs/contributing/patching-the-standard-library.md, "Patching a vendored module".

